This screenshot is captured at release time using a live VSCode instance.

It is not available in CI because this environment is headless (no display server).

What the screenshot shows:
- Hover over the `wait` keyword in a .ynz file in VSCode
- The hover popup displays the v0.3-M2 text:
    WHAT: "Suspends the calling function until the awaited expression completes.
          The OS thread is freed for other tasks during the suspension."
    WHAT INSTEAD: "Write `wait foo()` at a call site to suspend until `foo()` returns."
    WHY: "`wait` makes the function pause without blocking the OS thread..."
- A `wait print("hi")` line shows a yellow squiggle (WaitOnNonMayBlockWarning)
  with the message: "The function `print` does not contain a suspension point;
  `wait` here changes nothing."

To capture the real screenshot at release time:
1. Build: cargo build -p ynz-lsp --release
2. Open tooling/vscode-ynz/ in VSCode (F5 to launch extension host)
3. Open a .ynz file with `wait sleepAsync(100)` and `wait print("hi")`
4. Hover over `wait` and take a screenshot
5. Save as tooling/vscode-ynz/screenshots/wait-suspension.png
6. Delete this .PLACEHOLDER file
